  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-21T13:33:38.694Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If:\n- A physbone has Gravity enabled, and;\n- There exists a WD off workflow layer containing a state that would rotate that bone to a specific position;\nThen the physbone will \"vibrate\"/jitter visibly at random intervals. I believe the frequency of the jitters can depend on how complicated the avatar or animator controller are, but this is easy to confirm even in a barebones avatar with just one non-base FX layer and no additional bells and whistles (even if you can't visually observe the jitters minor variations in transform rotation can be observed in unity).\nNote that this is independent of \"Is animated\" being enabled or disabled. As far as I can tell, this issue depends only on Gravity. Removing Gravity keeps the bone from jittering.\nNote that this does not require the state that would rotate the bone to be active or even reachable. The mere presence, in the animator controller, of a state capable of rotating the bone, even if no transitions lead to it, will cause this issue. Removing that state will keep the bone from jittering.\nThis is problematic because it prevents setups in which bones would be reset to a specific position when the physbone component is disabled.",
